 ## Overview
-Ray-driven splatting is a hybrid volume rendering technique that combines the precomputation of splatting with the pixel-accurate accumulation of ray casting [S1, S2, unofficial]. It solves the problem of efficient perspective projection in splatting, where traditional methods struggle with the complexity of mapping 3D footprints to screen space [S2, unofficial]. Unlike [EWA Splatting](1069-ewa-splatting.md), which approximates footprints via elliptical weighting, ray-driven splatting spawns rays to intersect splats suspended in object space, enabling acceleration structures like early ray termination and bounding volumes [S1, S2, unofficial].
+Ray-driven splatting is a hybrid volume rendering technique that combines the precomputation of splatting with the accumulation logic of ray casting [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of inefficient and inaccurate perspective projection in traditional voxel-driven splatting, where mapping 3D footprints to the 2D image plane becomes complex and slow [S2, unofficial]. Unlike traditional splatting, which is sensitive to perspective transforms, this method spawns rays to intersect splats suspended in object space, enabling the use of ray-tracing optimizations like early ray termination and spatial acceleration structures [S2, unofficial].
 
